From ce9f82af9111a7514fdf9dda73bde88f34af5847 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:47:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 107/201] Gui: navigation cube edges and corners are easy to
 hit, and tooltips say what a click does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SoNaviCube::pickZones: a pick near the border of a face (the outer part of
each side) counts as the edge or corner next to it, so they are easy to
hit however thin their chamfer is drawn. On a grid over the cube, edges
are hit from 3.4 times the area and corners from twice the area.

A tooltip tells what a click on the part under the mouse does ('View from
the front, top and right corner', 'Turn up by 45°', 'Home view') and that
the cube can be dragged and double-clicked. Parameters PickZones and
ShowTips, on by default in the integrated environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
